                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Played through 4 levels so far, and each level is pretty big (I consider my self good in it, and with around 15 to minutes to finish a level) with still 7 levels to go, and so far the game is pretty neat!\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n7fhCspqiOU\n\nThe art style is pretty and clean, the controls are good but not great as it needs some less delay regarding grappling to orbs. I'd like to compared the grappling in this game with \"A Story About My Uncle\" with me saying that ASAMU's grappling is a lot more accurate and smoother regarding connecting with a surface/orb and just a general faster momentum from preforming long and distance jumps. While this game have a lot more complexity regarding the grapling mechanics and playthrough, I'm just hopeful that the basic nature of this mechanic gets a lot more refined.\n\nI didn't compare the game to Mirror's Edge because it's feels somewhat far from it, as Mirror's Edge core gameplay mechanic is its complex movement system, while Welkin Road's core gameplay is its complex grappling system.\n\nThe gist: It's a pretty good game and definitely worth the asking price from the looks of it. It's a \"pretty good game\" although not to the standards as I was hopping for, but it definitely can be =)",
